"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkcasdoor_website=globalThis.webpackChunkcasdoor_website||[]).push([[3532],{20900(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"casdoor-on-kubernetes","metadata":{"permalink":"/pt/blog/casdoor-on-kubernetes","editUrl":"https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor-website/edit/master/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-07-casdoor-on-kubernetes.mdx","source":"@site/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-07-casdoor-on-kubernetes.mdx","title":"Running Casdoor on Kubernetes: Official Helm Chart and Configuration as Code","description":"Casdoor has an official Helm chart. It lives in the main repository under manifests/casdoor, is published with every Casdoor release to GHCR, and is listed on Artifact Hub. Starting with Casdoor v4.18.0, the chart can also hold your organizations, applications, users and providers as declarative configuration: change them in the values file, run helm upgrade, and the running pods apply the change without a restart.","date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/casdoor"},{"inline":true,"label":"Kubernetes","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/kubernetes"},{"inline":true,"label":"Helm","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/helm"},{"inline":true,"label":"GitOps","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/git-ops"},{"inline":true,"label":"Configuration as Code","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/configuration-as-code"},{"inline":true,"label":"IAM","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/iam"},{"inline":true,"label":"SSO","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/sso"}],"readingTime":5.45,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Yang Luo","title":"Casdoor Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hsluoyz","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/hsluoyz","key":"hsluoyz","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"casdoor-on-kubernetes","title":"Running Casdoor on Kubernetes: Official Helm Chart and Configuration as Code","authors":["hsluoyz"],"tags":["Casdoor","Kubernetes","Helm","GitOps","Configuration as Code","IAM","SSO"],"date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Casdoor Joins CNCF Cloud Native Landscape","permalink":"/pt/blog/casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape"}},"content":"Casdoor has an official Helm chart. It lives in the main repository under [`manifests/casdoor`](https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor/tree/master/manifests/casdoor), is published with every Casdoor release to GHCR, and is listed on [Artifact Hub](https://artifacthub.io/packages/helm/casdoor/casdoor). Starting with Casdoor v4.18.0, the chart can also hold your organizations, applications, users and providers as declarative configuration: change them in the values file, run `helm upgrade`, and the running pods apply the change without a restart.\\n\\nThis post walks through a Kubernetes deployment from the first `helm install` to a setup you can keep in Git.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Install\\n\\nYou need Helm v3.8+ and a cluster:\\n\\n```shell\\nhelm install casdoor oci://ghcr.io/casdoor/helm-charts/casdoor\\n```\\n\\nThe chart version is the Casdoor version, so `--version 4.18.0` installs Casdoor 4.18.0. Without an Ingress or Gateway, the service is only reachable inside the cluster. To try it, forward a port:\\n\\n```shell\\nkubectl port-forward svc/casdoor 8000:8000\\n```\\n\\nThen open `http://localhost:8000` and sign in with `admin` / `123`.\\n\\n## A production setup\\n\\nThe defaults are meant for a quick try: Casdoor stores its data in SQLite inside the container, so it is lost when the pod is replaced. For a real deployment, put the settings below in a `values.yaml` file and install with `helm install casdoor oci://ghcr.io/casdoor/helm-charts/casdoor -f values.yaml`.\\n\\n### External database\\n\\n```yaml\\ndatabase:\\n  driver: postgres # or mysql, cockroachdb\\n  host: postgres.db.svc.cluster.local\\n  user: casdoor\\n  password: change-me\\n  databaseName: casdoor\\n  sslMode: require\\n```\\n\\nTo keep the database password out of the values file, put the whole `app.conf` in a Secret and set `configFromSecret` to its name.\\n\\n### Exposing Casdoor\\n\\nThe chart supports both a classic Ingress and the Gateway API. With an Ingress controller and cert-manager:\\n\\n```yaml\\ningress:\\n  enabled: true\\n  className: nginx\\n  annotations:\\n    cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: letsencrypt-prod\\n  hosts:\\n    - host: door.example.com\\n      paths:\\n        - path: /\\n          pathType: Prefix\\n  tls:\\n    - secretName: casdoor-tls\\n      hosts:\\n        - door.example.com\\n```\\n\\nWith the Gateway API (Istio, Envoy Gateway, Cilium, Kong, NGINX Gateway Fabric and others), attach an `HTTPRoute` to an existing Gateway:\\n\\n```yaml\\ngatewayApi:\\n  enabled: true\\n  parentRefs:\\n    - name: my-gateway\\n      namespace: gateway-system\\n  hostnames:\\n    - door.example.com\\n```\\n\\nThe chart can also create the Gateway itself and add an HTTP to HTTPS redirect, see the [Helm guide](/docs/basic/try-with-helm#exposing-casdoor).\\n\\n### More than one replica\\n\\nCasdoor keeps sign-in sessions on local disk by default. Before running more than one replica, point all of them to the same Redis, so a user stays signed in whichever pod serves the request. Every `app.conf` setting can be passed as an environment variable, so the endpoint can come from a Secret:\\n\\n```yaml\\nreplicaCount: 3\\n\\nenvFromSecret:\\n  - name: redisEndpoint\\n    secretName: casdoor-redis\\n    key: endpoint # host:port, or host:port,db,password\\n```\\n\\nThe same Redis is used for the OAuth device flow state. Once Redis is in place, `autoscaling.enabled: true` adds a HorizontalPodAutoscaler.\\n\\n## Configuration as code\\n\\nClicking organizations and applications together in the web UI is fine for a first test, but most teams want the setup of their identity provider reviewed and versioned like the rest of their infrastructure. The `initData` values do that:\\n\\n```yaml\\ninitData:\\n  enabled: true\\n  data:\\n    organizations:\\n      - owner: admin\\n        name: acme\\n        displayName: Acme\\n        passwordType: bcrypt\\n    applications:\\n      - owner: admin\\n        name: app-acme-portal\\n        organization: acme\\n        displayName: Acme Portal\\n        redirectUris:\\n          - https://portal.acme.example.com/callback\\n    users:\\n      - owner: acme\\n        name: alice\\n        displayName: Alice\\n        password: change-me\\n        signupApplication: app-acme-portal\\n    roles:\\n      - owner: acme\\n        name: admins\\n        displayName: Admins\\n        users: [acme/alice]\\n        isEnabled: true\\n```\\n\\nThe chart stores the data in a Secret and mounts it into the pods. Casdoor applies it at startup, then checks it every 30 seconds (`initData.watchInterval`). When you change the data and run `helm upgrade`, kubelet updates the mounted Secret and the running pods apply it without a restart.\\n\\nA few rules make this safe to use alongside the web UI:\\n\\n- **Only the fields you write are managed.** An object that already exists gets the fields set in the file; its other fields keep the values edited in the UI. You can manage just the redirect URIs of an application, and leave the rest to the admin console.\\n- **Passwords are initial passwords.** A user\'s `password` is only used when the user is created, so users can change theirs afterwards.\\n- **Nothing is deleted.** Removing an object from the file doesn\'t remove it from Casdoor.\\n- **Errors don\'t take Casdoor down.** If an object fails to apply, the error is logged and Casdoor keeps serving; the data is retried on every check until it applies.\\n\\nThe file format is the one Casdoor has always used for [data initialization](/docs/deployment/data-initialization): organizations, applications, users, providers, certs, roles, permissions, groups, LDAP servers, webhooks, plans, pricings and more, with the same field names as the REST API. A quick way to get started is to export an existing instance with `casdoor -export` and keep the objects you want to manage.\\n\\nTo keep the data out of the values file, for example when it is managed by Sealed Secrets or External Secrets, create the Secret yourself:\\n\\n```yaml\\ninitData:\\n  enabled: true\\n  existingSecret: casdoor-init-data\\n  existingSecretKey: init_data.yaml\\n```\\n\\nThe same feature works without Kubernetes. Mount a JSON or YAML file and set:\\n\\n```ini\\ninitDataFile = /init-data/init_data.yaml\\ninitDataMerge = true\\ninitDataWatchInterval = 30\\n```\\n\\n## Or use Terraform\\n\\nIf you prefer `terraform plan`, imports of existing objects and drift detection, the official [Terraform provider](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/casdoor/casdoor) manages the same objects through the Casdoor API:\\n\\n```terraform\\nresource \\"casdoor_application\\" \\"portal\\" {\\n  name          = \\"app-acme-portal\\"\\n  organization  = \\"acme\\"\\n  redirect_uris = [\\"https://portal.acme.example.com/callback\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\nUse the Helm values when the configuration should ship with the deployment, and Terraform when Casdoor is one of many systems you already manage with it. See the [Terraform guide](/docs/deployment/terraform).\\n\\n## Coming from the old chart\\n\\nUp to v4.15.0, the chart was published as `oci://registry-1.docker.io/casbin/casdoor-helm-charts`, and the separate `casdoor/casdoor-helm` repository is now archived. The Docker Hub chart still receives every release, but new installs should use the GHCR one. Moving an existing release over is a regular upgrade, and resource names stay the same:\\n\\n```shell\\nhelm upgrade casdoor oci://ghcr.io/casdoor/helm-charts/casdoor --version <version>\\n```\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- Helm chart: [Artifact Hub](https://artifacthub.io/packages/helm/casdoor/casdoor) \xb7 [source](https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor/tree/master/manifests/casdoor)\\n- Guides: [Try with Helm](/docs/basic/try-with-helm) \xb7 [Data initialization and configuration as code](/docs/deployment/data-initialization#configuration-as-code) \xb7 [Terraform](/docs/deployment/terraform)\\n- Don\'t want to run it yourself? [Casdoor Cloud](https://www.casdoor.com/pricing?utm_source=casdoor.ai&utm_medium=blog&utm_content=kubernetes) gives you a dedicated Casdoor instance that we host and keep upgraded for you."},{"id":"casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape","metadata":{"permalink":"/pt/blog/casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape","editUrl":"https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor-website/edit/master/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-22-casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape.mdx","source":"@site/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-22-casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape.mdx","title":"Casdoor Joins CNCF Cloud Native Landscape","description":"On February 22, 2026, Casdoor joined the CNCF Cloud Native Landscape, under the Security & Compliance category in Provisioning. The Landscape brings together widely used cloud-native projects and products; inclusion helps users and enterprises discover and evaluate solutions for building cloud-native systems.","date":"2026-02-22T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/casdoor"},{"inline":true,"label":"CNCF","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/cncf"},{"inline":true,"label":"Cloud Native","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/cloud-native"},{"inline":true,"label":"Landscape","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/landscape"},{"inline":true,"label":"IAM","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/iam"},{"inline":true,"label":"SSO","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/sso"},{"inline":true,"label":"Security","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":1.95,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Yang Luo","title":"Casdoor Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/hsluoyz","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/hsluoyz","key":"hsluoyz","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape","title":"Casdoor Joins CNCF Cloud Native Landscape","authors":["hsluoyz"],"tags":["Casdoor","CNCF","Cloud Native","Landscape","IAM","SSO","Security"],"date":"2026-02-22T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Running Casdoor on Kubernetes: Official Helm Chart and Configuration as Code","permalink":"/pt/blog/casdoor-on-kubernetes"},"nextItem":{"title":"Melhorando a Seguran\xe7a do Aplicativo e a Experi\xeancia do Usu\xe1rio com o SSO de Autentica\xe7\xe3o Facial do Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/face-authentication-casdoor-sso"}},"content":"On February 22, 2026, **Casdoor** joined the [CNCF Cloud Native Landscape](https://landscape.cncf.io/), under the **Security & Compliance** category in Provisioning. The Landscape brings together widely used cloud-native projects and products; inclusion helps users and enterprises discover and evaluate solutions for building cloud-native systems.\\n\\n[https://landscape.cncf.io/?item=provisioning--security-compliance--casdoor](https://landscape.cncf.io/?item=provisioning--security-compliance--casdoor)\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n<img src=\\"/img/blog/cncf-landscape-casdoor.png\\" alt=\\"Casdoor on CNCF Landscape - Security and Compliance section\\" style={{maxWidth: \'100%\', height: \'auto\', border: \'1px solid #eee\', borderRadius: \'8px\'}} />\\n\\n_Casdoor on the CNCF Cloud Native Landscape (Security & Compliance)_\\n\\n## Sobre o Casdoor\\n\\n<div style={{display: \'flex\', alignItems: \'center\', gap: \'1rem\', flexWrap: \'wrap\', marginBottom: \'1rem\'}}>\\n\\n<img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/casdoor-logo_1185x256.png\\" alt=\\"Casdoor\\" style={{height: \'80px\', width: \'auto\'}} />\\n\\n</div>\\n\\nCasdoor is an open-source, UI-first Identity and Access Management (IAM) / Single Sign-On (SSO) platform with a web UI. It supports OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML, and CAS, as well as many social logins (Google, GitHub, WeChat, etc.), and helps you build user management and SSO in a few steps. Casdoor is developed by [Casbin](https://casbin.org) in Golang and React. It uses a front-end/back-end separation architecture, supports high concurrency, and is actively maintained by the community. The project has received over 13k GitHub stars.\\n\\n## About CNCF and the Cloud Native Landscape\\n\\n<div style={{display: \'flex\', alignItems: \'center\', gap: \'1.5rem\', flexWrap: \'wrap\', marginBottom: \'1rem\'}}>\\n\\n<img src=\\"https://www.cncf.io/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/cncf-main-site-logo.svg\\" alt=\\"CNCF - Cloud Native Computing Foundation\\" style={{height: \'80px\', width: \'auto\'}} />\\n<img src=\\"https://landscape.cncf.io/images/logo_header.svg\\" alt=\\"CNCF Cloud Native Landscape\\" style={{height: \'80px\', width: \'auto\'}} />\\n\\n</div>\\n\\nThe **Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF)** is a Linux Foundation project that promotes cloud-native technologies. Its vision is to make cloud native ubiquitous. CNCF maintains the **Cloud Native Landscape** ([https://landscape.cncf.io](https://landscape.cncf.io)), which classifies and tracks projects and products in the cloud-native ecosystem and serves as a reference map for developers and enterprises.\\n\\n## Looking ahead\\n\\nJoining the CNCF Landscape reflects progress in Casdoor\u2019s maturity and community. We will keep improving Casdoor and its integration with cloud-native workflows, and we welcome more users and contributors to join the community.\\n\\nLinks relacionados:\\n\\n- [Casdoor](https://casdoor.org) \xb7 [GitHub](https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor) \xb7 [Documentation](https://casdoor.org/docs) \xb7 [CNCF Landscape \u2013 Casdoor](https://landscape.cncf.io/?selected=casdoor)"},{"id":"face-authentication-casdoor-sso","metadata":{"permalink":"/pt/blog/face-authentication-casdoor-sso","editUrl":"https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor-website/edit/master/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2023-12-12-face-authentication-casdoor-sso.mdx","source":"@site/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2023-12-12-face-authentication-casdoor-sso.mdx","title":"Melhorando a Seguran\xe7a do Aplicativo e a Experi\xeancia do Usu\xe1rio com o SSO de Autentica\xe7\xe3o Facial do Casdoor","description":"Em uma era onde a gest\xe3o de identidade digital \xe9 crucial, solu\xe7\xf5es de Single Sign-On (SSO) como o Casdoor est\xe3o revolucionando a maneira como os usu\xe1rios interagem com m\xfaltiplos aplicativos. O SSO do Casdoor simplifica o processo de login permitindo que os usu\xe1rios se autentiquem apenas uma vez para acessar m\xfaltiplos servi\xe7os. Isso n\xe3o apenas aumenta a conveni\xeancia do usu\xe1rio, mas tamb\xe9m impulsiona o engajamento e a satisfa\xe7\xe3o.","date":"2023-12-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/casdoor"},{"inline":true,"label":"SSO","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/sso"},{"inline":true,"label":"Single-Sign-On","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/single-sign-on"},{"inline":true,"label":"Face Recogniztion","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/face-recogniztion"},{"inline":true,"label":"FaceID","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/face-id"},{"inline":true,"label":"Face","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/face"},{"inline":true,"label":"Machine Learning","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/machine-learning"}],"readingTime":1.94,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"James Lawson","title":"Gerente de Produto","url":"https://casdoor.org","imageURL":"https://cdn.casbin.com/casdoor/static/admin.png","key":"James Lawson","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"face-authentication-casdoor-sso","title":"Melhorando a Seguran\xe7a do Aplicativo e a Experi\xeancia do Usu\xe1rio com o SSO de Autentica\xe7\xe3o Facial do Casdoor","authors":["James Lawson"],"tags":["Casdoor","SSO","Single-Sign-On","Face Recogniztion","FaceID","Face","Machine Learning"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Casdoor Joins CNCF Cloud Native Landscape","permalink":"/pt/blog/casdoor-joins-cncf-landscape"},"nextItem":{"title":"Bem-vindo","permalink":"/pt/blog/welcome"}},"content":"Em uma era onde a gest\xe3o de identidade digital \xe9 crucial, solu\xe7\xf5es de Single Sign-On (SSO) como o Casdoor est\xe3o revolucionando a maneira como os usu\xe1rios interagem com m\xfaltiplos aplicativos. O SSO do Casdoor simplifica o processo de login permitindo que os usu\xe1rios se autentiquem apenas uma vez para acessar m\xfaltiplos servi\xe7os. Isso n\xe3o apenas aumenta a conveni\xeancia do usu\xe1rio, mas tamb\xe9m impulsiona o engajamento e a satisfa\xe7\xe3o.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nPara as empresas, o SSO do Casdoor racionaliza a gest\xe3o de credenciais dos usu\xe1rios, melhorando a seguran\xe7a e simplificando a integra\xe7\xe3o de novos usu\xe1rios. Ele contraria o risco associado a senhas fracas ou recicladas centralizando a gest\xe3o de usu\xe1rios.\\n\\nNo entanto, diante das crescentes amea\xe7as online, integrar medidas de seguran\xe7a robustas em sistemas SSO como o Casdoor \xe9 vital. \xc9 aqui que a tecnologia de autentica\xe7\xe3o facial entra em jogo, adicionando uma camada extra de prote\xe7\xe3o enquanto mant\xe9m intera\xe7\xf5es amig\xe1veis com o usu\xe1rio.\\n\\nA autentica\xe7\xe3o facial emprega caracter\xedsticas faciais \xfanicas para confirmar as identidades dos usu\xe1rios. Ela compara imagens ao vivo com modelos faciais armazenados, oferecendo uma maneira segura e simples de autenticar usu\xe1rios. Este m\xe9todo possui alta precis\xe3o, mesmo sob condi\xe7\xf5es variadas, e \xe9 amplamente adotado em dispositivos modernos do consumidor.\\n\\nIntegrar a autentica\xe7\xe3o facial no sistema SSO do Casdoor promete uma experi\xeancia de usu\xe1rio segura, eficiente e cont\xednua. Para garantir um desempenho \xf3timo, \xe9 crucial focar em:\\n\\n1. _Medidas Anti-Spoofing_: Implementar detec\xe7\xe3o de vivacidade, como rastreamento de movimentos dos olhos ou gestos aleat\xf3rios, \xe9 essencial para contrariar tentativas de spoofing e manter a integridade do sistema.\\n\\n2. _Atualiza\xe7\xf5es Regulares para Melhorar a Precis\xe3o_: Manter a tecnologia de autentica\xe7\xe3o facial atualizada com os \xfaltimos avan\xe7os em IA e biometria garante precis\xe3o e melhora a experi\xeancia do usu\xe1rio. \xc9 vital usar conjuntos de dados diversos para o treinamento de algoritmos para prevenir vieses.\\n\\n3. _Equilibrando Seguran\xe7a e Conveni\xeancia_: Os melhores sistemas encontram um equil\xedbrio perfeito entre medidas de seguran\xe7a rigorosas e a conveni\xeancia do usu\xe1rio. Essa abordagem incentiva a ado\xe7\xe3o do usu\xe1rio garantindo um processo de autentica\xe7\xe3o direto sem comprometer a seguran\xe7a.\\n\\nEm conclus\xe3o, integrando a autentica\xe7\xe3o facial com o SSO do Casdoor, as empresas podem oferecer uma experi\xeancia de login segura, eficiente e amig\xe1vel ao usu\xe1rio. Isso n\xe3o apenas fortalece a seguran\xe7a, mas tamb\xe9m est\xe1 alinhado com as expectativas modernas dos usu\xe1rios no mundo digital."},{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/pt/blog/welcome","editUrl":"https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor-website/edit/master/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2021-08-24-welcome.mdx","source":"@site/i18n/pt/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2021-08-24-welcome.mdx","title":"Bem-vindo","description":"Bem-vindo ao site oficial do Casdoor!\ud83d\udc4b","date":"2021-08-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/casdoor"},{"inline":true,"label":"SSO","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/sso"},{"inline":true,"label":"Authentication","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/authentication"},{"inline":true,"label":"OAuth2.0","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/o-auth-2-0"},{"inline":true,"label":"Casbin","permalink":"/pt/blog/tags/casbin"}],"readingTime":1.5,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"ErikQQY","title":"Membro do Casbin","url":"https://github.com/ErikQQY","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52615090?s=120&v=4","key":"ErikQQY","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Bem-vindo","authors":["ErikQQY"],"tags":["Casdoor","SSO","Authentication","OAuth2.0","Casbin"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Melhorando a Seguran\xe7a do Aplicativo e a Experi\xeancia do Usu\xe1rio com o SSO de Autentica\xe7\xe3o Facial do Casdoor","permalink":"/pt/blog/face-authentication-casdoor-sso"}},"content":"Bem-vindo ao site oficial do Casdoor!\ud83d\udc4b\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## O que \xe9 o Casdoor?\\n\\nCasdoor is a UI-first [Identity Access Management (IAM)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Identity_management) / [Single-Sign-On (SSO)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_sign-on) platform based on OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML and CAS.\\n\\nCasdoor is developed by [Casbin](https://casbin.org) using Golang and React.\\n\\nO Casdoor visa fornecer uma plataforma de autentica\xe7\xe3o poderosa para lidar com o gerenciamento de usu\xe1rios.\\n\\n## Por que usar o Casdoor?\\n\\n- \u26a1\ufe0f Recurso poderoso e configura\xe7\xe3o simples. With support for  <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_google.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_github.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_facebook.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_twitter.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_linkedin.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_weibo.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_wechat.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_qq.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_dingtalk.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img>   <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_gitee.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img>  <img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_wecom.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img><img src=\\"https://cdn.casbin.org/img/social_gitlab.png\\" width=\\"30\\"></img> sign in and traditional username/password sign in, Casdoor helps you implement your users management system just in a few steps.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udca5 Arquitetura de separa\xe7\xe3o front-end back-end. O Casdoor fornece uma UI manobr\xe1vel e suporta alta concorr\xeancia.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd42 Comunidade open source ativa. O Casdoor \xe9 open source e mantido ativamente.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf10 Suporte a m\xfaltiplos idiomas. O Casdoor suporta v\xe1rios idiomas, incluindo chin\xeas, ingl\xeas, franc\xeas e muitos outros.\\n\\n## Como usar o Casdoor?\\n\\nYou can follow the detailed document to learn about [Casdoor API](https://door.casdoor.com/swagger/) and [setup your own Casdoor](/docs/basic/server-installation). Or use the [Casdoor SDKs](/docs/how-to-connect/sdk) to implement your own application."}]}}')}}]);